{
 "id": 44,
 "number": 23,
 "title": "Merge k Sorted Lists",
 "slug": "merge-k-sorted-lists",
 "category": "linked-list",
 "difficulty": "Hard",
 "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/merge-k-sorted-lists/",
 "pattern": "Min-heap of the list fronts",
 "statement": "You are given `k` linked lists, each sorted in increasing order. Merge them all into **one** sorted linked list and return it.",
 "example": {
  "input": "lists = [[1,4],[2,5],[3]]",
  "output": "[1,2,3,4,5]",
  "why": "Taking the smallest front node again and again gives 1, 2, 3, 4, 5."
 },
 "more": [
  {
   "input": "lists = [[1,4,5],[1,3,4],[2,6]]",
   "output": "[1,1,2,3,4,4,5,6]"
  },
  {
   "input": "lists = []",
   "output": "[]"
  },
  {
   "input": "lists = [None]",
   "output": "[]"
  }
 ],
 "idea": [
  "The next node of the merged list is always the smallest among the **current front nodes** of the k lists.",
  "Finding that smallest by scanning all k fronts costs O(k) every time. A **min-heap** holding one entry per list finds it in O(log k).",
  "Pop the smallest, append it to the result, and push the next node from the same list (if there is one). The heap never holds more than k entries."
 ],
 "code": "import heapq\n\nclass Solution:\n    def mergeKLists(self, lists: List[ListNode]) -> ListNode:\n        min_heap = []\n        for i, l in enumerate(lists):\n            if l:\n                heapq.heappush(min_heap, (l.val, i))\n\n        dummy = ListNode()\n        current = dummy\n\n        while min_heap:\n            val, idx = heapq.heappop(min_heap)\n            current.next = ListNode(val)\n            current = current.next\n            if lists[idx].next:\n                heapq.heappush(min_heap, (lists[idx].next.val, idx))\n                lists[idx] = lists[idx].next\n\n        return dummy.next",
 "complexity": {
  "time": "O(N log k)",
  "timeWhy": "Each of the N nodes is pushed and popped once from a heap of at most k entries.",
  "space": "O(k)",
  "spaceWhy": "The heap holds one entry per list (this version also builds new nodes for the result)."
 },
